refusals.template:
refusing to start — decision 0111 retired these process variables, and a set one would be ignored in silence:
{set}
Unset them and run again. Nothing was read and nothing was written.

--local runs the engine on this machine from a profile FILE, and there is no project above the working directory to stage one in.
{staging_reason}
Run inside your project (or set $VIKE_SETTINGS_DIR), pass an already-merged profile to --profile, or write one first with --write-profile <path>

the recording profile and this server disagree about the store root, and since the recorder merged into the data daemon (ruling 10) there is only one:
  profile `store` = {profile}
  server root    = {server}
One process owns venue connections, the store and serving, so a recording that landed in the first would be invisible to every query answered from the second. Point them at one directory — change the profile's `store` (⚠ WHICH profile: a `--record` file, or the `recorder` ROW a `--recorder-profile` names; the refusal above this one names the origin this process actually read), or write the profile's path to the server's row (`vike-cli config set config.store_root <path>`) — and start again. Both paths above are shown as this process resolved them, absolute against its working directory; a symlink that makes two spellings the same directory is still refused, because this comparison is textual by design (canonicalising would require a store root that may not exist yet).
